WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.920
Evidence preservation begins before acquisition.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:16.260
Initial handling should document the device condition as found: physical state, power state, lock state, visible notifications, network indicators, connected accessories, SIM or removable media presence, and any obvious damage.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:22.160
Photographs and notes matter because the condition at first contact can affect later interpretation.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.500
Network isolation is a consideration, not a reflex.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:33.320
Investigators may need to prevent remote wiping, new messages, sync changes, or other network activity, but changing network state can also affect evidence.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:38.740
The right action depends on authority, policy, case context, and device condition.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.120
The key is to document what was done, why it was done, and when it was done.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:48.540
Chain of custody records who handled evidence, when, why, and under what conditions.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.120
This is more than paperwork.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:55.300
It helps show that the evidence was controlled and that changes were minimized or explained.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:03.920
Each transfer, examination, storage location, and acquisition action should be recorded in a way that another qualified person can understand later.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.340
Acquisition concepts are best understood at a high level.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:15.720
Logical acquisition collects accessible files, records, backups, or structured data through supported methods or forensic tools.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:22.660
File system acquisition may collect a broader view of files and application data when lawful access and technical conditions allow.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.400
Cloud or account-based acquisition may collect data from provider services or authorized account exports.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.300
Each approach has scope, limits, and legal implications.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:37.400
Acquisition choices shape what evidence is available and how defensible the conclusions are.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:45.380
A method may collect messages but not deleted data, media but not app-private databases, or cloud records but not local device context.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:52.000
Strong reports explain what was acquired, what was not acquired, what tools were used, and what limitations remain.
